WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.260
AI gets stuck on everything now.

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:07.340
Collars, tractors, the app
that says rain on Thursday.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:08.750
So what does it mean?

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.577
Under the label there are
really three kinds of tool.

00:00:12.597 --> 00:00:17.560
Once you can tell them apart, the sales
pitch gets a lot easier to judge.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.933
The first kind is AI that senses.

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:24.320
It takes readings from the
world and spots a pattern.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:28.080
A collar notices a cow's
rumination time has dropped.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.970
A camera on a sprayer
tells a weed from a crop.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.690
The second kind is AI that predicts.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:40.783
It learns from years of past numbers
and makes a call about what comes next.

00:00:40.803 --> 00:00:44.197
Pasture growth, the
weather, lambing dates.

00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:47.823
What you get is a best guess
with some spread either side.

00:00:47.843 --> 00:00:48.860
It's never a

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.380
promise.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.500
The third kind is AI
that writes and talks.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:00.420
ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, Copilot,
Amazon Quick and others.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:04.900
You ask a question in normal words,
and it answers in normal words.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.753
This is what most people mean by AI now.

00:01:07.773 --> 00:01:11.270
And it's what this course
spends most of its time on.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.390
Try a quick test.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.990
A collar that flags a cow on heat?

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:17.470
That's sensing.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:20.190
A forecast that says rain on Thursday?

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.390
Predicting.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:24.430
Your phone turning your
voice into a text message?

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.560
Writing and talking.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:30.120
So how does a chat AI
come up with an answer?

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.840
It learned from a huge amount of text.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.840
Websites, books, manuals, forum posts.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:40.890
From all of it, it learned which
words tend to follow which.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:43.410
Try finishing this sentence.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:47.090
After weaning, we moved
the ewes back onto the...

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:49.970
You probably thought hill, or back block.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:51.620
Not beach.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.687
A chat AI does the same thing, very fast.

00:01:55.707 --> 00:02:00.220
It writes one small piece at a time,
and each time it picks a likely next

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.630
word.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.683
That one idea explains a lot.

00:02:04.703 --> 00:02:09.137
It has taken in so much that its
likely words are often useful.

00:02:09.157 --> 00:02:13.083
So it writes clear text, and
explains things plainly.

00:02:13.103 --> 00:02:16.203
But a likely answer
isn't always a true one.

00:02:16.223 --> 00:02:20.520
When it doesn't know, it still
writes something that sounds right.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:24.373
Some apps can search the web,
or read a file you give them,

00:02:24.393 --> 00:02:25.760
and that helps.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:29.040
They still write the answer
by picking likely words.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.120
So the habit stays the same.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.170
Check what matters.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:38.010
Below the video, sort some farm
tools into the three kinds.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:42.460
Then we'll look at where AI already
turns up on New Zealand farms.
